Optional tcp_save_synack core integration (ebpf addon, HTTP upstreams).

Apply to Nginx, then configure with --add-module=/path/to/ja4-nginx-module/ebpf
to enable the feature. Independent of the client TCP_SAVE_SYN patch.

New fields are appended after existing members, and builds with the addon add
a module signature bit, so --with-compat modules built without it are refused
instead of reading shifted structures.

diff --git a/src/core/ngx_connection.c b/src/core/ngx_connection.c
--- a/src/core/ngx_connection.c
+++ b/src/core/ngx_connection.c
@@ -1346,6 +1346,10 @@ ngx_close_connection(ngx_connection_t *c)
         return;
     }
 
+#if (NGX_HAVE_EBPF)
+    ngx_connection_cleanup_synack(c);
+#endif
+
     if (c->read->timer_set) {
         ngx_del_timer(c->read);
     }
